[360.517, "maining limitations after round 4.**                                                                           \r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;36;138;61m 61 +\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m- **Every position costs one full weight stream** of about 438 MB at about 59 GB/s, roughly 7.3 ms on this M1. That\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;36;138;61m    +\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m is the floor for batch size 1 with float32 weights. LOGITS, FIXED and prompt processing now scale linearly at that\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;36;138;61m    +\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m rate.                                                                                                             \r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;36;138;61m 62 +\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m- The round-2 and round-3 analyses of decode (blocked transposed `sgemv` at the bandwidth ceiling, hybrid attention\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;36;138;61m    +\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m, tokenizer, load) still apply. The prefill-GEMM analyses no longer apply.                                         \r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;36;138;61m 63 +\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m- All earlier limitations (numerics within 3.1e-5 of the reference, load page fa"]
