[361.263, "                                                                                   \r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[2m67 \u001b[22m ## Round 3: profiling and optimisation\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 68 \u001b[22m \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;36;138;61m\u001b[48;2;220;255;220m 69 +\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m*(Historical. The chunked prefill described in rounds 1\u20133 violated rule 1 and was removed in round 4. P\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;36;138;61m    +\u001b[38;2;51;51;51mrefill, LOGITS and FIXED figures in these sections are not valid results.)*                            \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;36;138;61m\u001b[48;2;220;255;220m 70 +\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m                                                                                                       \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[2m 71 \u001b[22m The workloads are the same supplied fixtures, run with `prof/dev.py` and `prof/ab.py` (alternating bina\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m    \u001b[22m ries, medians) as in round 2. I also used `prof/ttft.py` to measure time to first token against decode \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B   \u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m    \u001b[22m step time"]
